# Development Standards — Forms

Module-structure region templates (common / object-manager / form modules) — `module-structure.md`. This file covers **form-presentation** rules only.

## Programmatic Modification of Typical Forms

All typical form modifications are performed **programmatically**, not visually. Elements are created in `OnCreateAtServer` handler (or via subscription / extension).

## Placement of Added Elements

- If the form has tabs — add elements to a separate tab (e.g. "Additional" or with `{PREFIX}`).
- If no tabs — create a group without title for added elements.
- Typical form element names — with `{PREFIX}` prefix.

## New Forms (Non-Typical Objects)

- Separate header attributes and tabular sections into distinct tabs: "Main" (header), then one tab per tabular section.
- Fill "Header Data Path" property for pages with tabular sections.
- Reference fields — maximum width 27 characters.
- Multiline comment fields — width 79, height 3.

## Fill Checking

- Use "Fill check" property on form attributes.
- Before writing / posting, call `ПроверитьЗаполнение()`:

```bsl
Если Не ПроверитьЗаполнение() Тогда
	Возврат;
КонецЕсли;
```

## Form Commands

- When creating commands that modify data — enable "Modifies stored data" flag.

## Form UX (project-delta)

Adapted from [dev-rules forms.md](https://github.com/yellow-hammer/dev-rules/blob/main/docs/forms.md) (CC-BY-SA 4.0 — see `1commerce-bsp-integration-checklists.mdc → Sources`). Full BSP hook checklists — `1commerce-bsp-integration-checklists.mdc`.

### Visibility and availability

- Centralize form element visibility/availability in one server procedure (e.g. `ОбновитьВидимостьДоступностьЭлементовФормы`) called from relevant event handlers — avoid scattering `Элементы.*.Видимость` across many handlers.
- Prefer **boolean expressions** in `Видимость` / `Доступность` properties when the condition is a simple predicate.

### Naming conventions for added UI containers

- Service tab for extension-specific fields: `{PREFIX}СтраницаСпециальная` (or `{PREFIX}ГруппаСпециальная` when tabs are absent).
- Follow existing project patterns discovered via `search_forms` before inventing new container names.

### List forms

- When the standard list form supports user settings — place filters in `ГруппаПользовательскихНастроек` rather than ad-hoc top-level groups.

### Document forms — selection UX

- For tabular-section row selection — prefer the configuration's standard pick pattern (`Подбор` / `Заполнить` commands) over custom one-off dialogs unless the task explicitly requires otherwise.
